WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.179
It all began long before we learned to
count time.

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.284
More than thirteen thousand years ago,

3
00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:10.939
our earliest ancestors began to walk and
observe.

4
00:00:11.406 --> 00:00:12.957
They watched the stars.

5
00:00:13.256 --> 00:00:17.877
They began to understand them and, through
them, to understand time.

6
00:00:18.454 --> 00:00:21.938
They listened to the wind, the birds and
the waters.

7
00:00:22.301 --> 00:00:26.351
They recognized the cycles of the sun, the
moon and the earth.

8
00:00:26.857 --> 00:00:28.878
They turned their attention inward.

9
00:00:29.256 --> 00:00:31.908
They observed their breath, their
heartbeat,

10
00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.150
their emotions and their thoughts.

11
00:00:34.526 --> 00:00:36.565
They learned about their own nature,

12
00:00:36.754 --> 00:00:40.339
their essence and that which gives meaning
to our lives.

13
00:00:40.836 --> 00:00:42.554
That knowledge lives on.

14
00:00:43.262 --> 00:00:44.262
Tonalamatl.

15
00:00:44.628 --> 00:00:49.000
The timekeeping tradition of ancient
Mexico.
